gate:
`make gate` ran in the worktree before every one of the 13 commits and passed each time. Every run printed "PASS: every KN5000 image assembles" and "PASS: every rebuilt ROM is byte-identical" (9/9 IDENTICAL).

Perturbation proof, once: I changed VoiceCtrlR1_Entry_001's clamp_max from 11 to 12 in the v9 macro form. The gate went red with "kn5000_v9_program 1 BYTES DIFFER" at exactly 0xEDBAC8 (0x0B vs 0x0C). I then restored it and v9 was IDENTICAL again.

`python3 scripts/analysis/assert_comments_preserved.py` was run on every commit. The only comments lost were deliberate, and each commit message explains them:
- the false v7 Naka_PresentationRootState note;
- 8 "Widget N (0x0N) / Screen group 7, index N" lines, proven false by the test1 link check;
- rewordings of this lane's own generated comments;
- fragments of .ascii literals that the checker misreads as comments.

The integrator's ownership check from main 23d1cb63 (`lane_worklists.py --verify-branch ext 3958235e s2/ext`) prints "VERIFY-BRANCH ext PASS (12 paths changed)": 6 owned .s files plus 6 new scripts.

